content.text:
An Opus worker is now rewriting the report's section 6, "What it cost". The new section gives:

- one entry per phase, from the item-31 incident through the audit, the two clarity rewrites, the scrape, the follow-up, the orientation, the ledger work and the skill changes, to the post-mortem report itself;
- for each phase, what its workers wrote and what I wrote in the same hours;
- the totals, and what the window took of your weekly limit.

The worker reuses the scout's measured figures. It measures only what the scout didn't split: the 3.7M of "other workers", the 3.42M of headless sessions, and my own 4.26M. When it's done, I'll republish the page at the same link.

At the record's rate of about 1.1M per percent, 3% is about 3.3M. What's running, with what each has written so far:

- the walk probe: 0.29M, estimate 0.8M;
- the demos probe: 0.08M, estimate 0.5M;
- the skill-history scout: 0.27M, estimate 0.3M;
- the cost section: 0.05M, estimate about 0.3M.

That leaves about 1.5M of work still to come. The ~1.8M of room left let me start one more task: an Opus worker that fixes the export probe's findings now. It will:
- make the distance stage show a library that doesn't parse, instead of reading it as 0;
- fix the error-sorting pattern for prefix operators;
- file the export check's three defects as ledger rows.

The batch planner still waits for the reset. It costs about 1.2M, and it needs the walk and demos reports first.

